# LOCAL VERSION OVERRIDES - an OPTIONAL, NORMALLY EMPTY file.
#
# NOTHING READS THIS FILE ANY MORE. It used to hold every gateway's pinned image / repo / commit,
# which made it a shared file naming every gateway in the field. The pins moved into each gateway's
# own directory, the shell runners that `source`d this file were deleted with the shell engine
# (cc630b7), and the gateway.sh manifests went in 1127cf1. Assigning a variable here has no effect.
#
# WHERE A PIN LIVES NOW:
#
#     gateways/<name>/definition.json   launch.image - a container image, pinned by TAG (no digest)
#     gateways/<name>/build.sh          COMMIT="${<NAME>_COMMIT:-<sha>}" - the source-built entrants
#
# The runner stamps the image tag, or the commit actually built, into every run JSON (`build`
# field), so the output discloses what was measured. If a pin should CHANGE, change it in that
# gateway's own directory, in a commit that says why. Do not add per-gateway lines here: this is a
# shared file and must name no entrant (a review rule; the lint that checked it was deleted).
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE. Envoy AI Gateway is intentionally NOT in this benchmark: it is Kubernetes-native
# (Envoy Gateway + CRDs, a full cluster), not a single-box drop-in, which is out of scope for this
# harness. That is a statement about a project with no directory here, so it names nothing in the field.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
